From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: iio: imu: st_lsm6dsx: the L018's LSM6DSV answers WHO_AM_I 0x71

The accelerometer at 0x6a on the L018's twi2 answers WHO_AM_I 0x71, and
st_lsm6dsx refused it ("unsupported whoami [71]"; mainline knows 0x70 for
the LSM6DSV and the LSM6DSV16X). The L018's vendor kernel drives this
part with ST's LSM6DSV register API (lsm6dsv_reg: eis, sflp, dual fsm)
after a check for exactly 0x71 (lsm6dsv_detect_init: cmp r3, #113), read
off that kernel on 25.10.2026.

So "st,lsm6dsv" accepts 0x71 as well as 0x70. No other compatible and no
other ID changes; only the L018 tree names st,lsm6dsv.

Measured on the L018, 25.10.2026 (module rebuilt with this change and
reloaded): lsm6dsv_accel and lsm6dsv_gyro come up; at rest x -14791,
y -140, z 8262 at 0.000598205 m/s2 per count - 10.1 m/s2, gravity.

diff -ruN a/drivers/iio/imu/st_lsm6dsx/st_lsm6dsx_core.c b/drivers/iio/imu/st_lsm6dsx/st_lsm6dsx_core.c
--- a/drivers/iio/imu/st_lsm6dsx/st_lsm6dsx_core.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/imu/st_lsm6dsx/st_lsm6dsx_core.c
@@ -1603,7 +1603,13 @@
 		return err;
 	}
 
-	if (data != st_lsm6dsx_sensor_settings[i].id[j].wai) {
+	/*
+	 * The LSM6DSV of the L018 projector answers 0x71, and its vendor kernel
+	 * drives it with ST's LSM6DSV register API after checking for exactly
+	 * 0x71 (lsm6dsv_detect_init, read off that kernel 25.10.2026).
+	 */
+	if (data != st_lsm6dsx_sensor_settings[i].id[j].wai &&
+	    !(id == ST_LSM6DSV_ID && data == 0x71)) {
 		dev_err(hw->dev, "unsupported whoami [%02x]\n", data);
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
